They were NOT identical for a while - Longfellow carried the pre-redirect
version - and nothing noticed, because the staged copy was placed beside the
vendored one and never compared. TestVendoredVectorsAgreeWithLongfellow (a
zknative test, since Longfellow's copy only exists in that build) now compares
them in full. It allowed the gap explicitly while it lasted and asserted the
exemption would expire; it did, and the comparison is total.

Re-vendor rather than edit. A local change turns a cross-implementation check
into a self-consistency one that passes while the verifier and the provers
disagree - which is the single failure this file exists to prevent.
